 ## Social Tool Strategy
 
-- Final text alone is never delivered to the group. To actually speak, call `social_send` (each part is delivered when passed as `parts`) or `message` with channel=telegram.
-- Read before replying: `social_get_state` → `social_read_messages` → `social_mark_read`, then `social_wait` when idle instead of polling.
-- Private `t.me/c/…` group links are not readable by me — never claim to have seen one; ask for pasted text, a forward, or a screenshot and view images with `social_get_media` by message_id.
-- Budget is max 6 sends/hour per group; on "hourly send budget exhausted" fall back to the `message` tool rather than retrying.
-- If a pasted checklist or answer "didn't arrive", assume the send tool was never called.
-- Topic-scoped sends (`telegram:-1003760551468:topic:<id>`) have been rejected with `platform rejected send` even after retries; the bare scope `telegram:-1003760551468` works. If a scope keeps failing, post once to the bare scope instead of retrying the topic.
-- After a dedupe/rejected-prefix error (`request rejected, do not repeat the confirmed prefix`), don't resend the same wording — say it differently or briefly.
-- Back-to-back `social_send` hits "send cooldown is active", and it can also fail with a bare `{"status":"failed"}`; in both cases switch to `message` (channel=telegram, chat_id=-1003760551468) instead of retrying.
-- A `queued` send status is not proof of delivery; if the user says it didn't arrive, rephrase rather than resending the identical text.
-- `social_wait`: pass only `purpose` + `seconds`, sleeping in `seconds` increments. Rejected by the ops limit: `seconds` above ~7200 ("wait duration exceeds the operator limit"), an over-large `quiet_seconds`, an absolute `until` hours ahead, and `purpose="messages"/"reply"` combined with `sleeping=true`. For a long sleep use `sleeping=true` + `seconds` (+ `on_timeout=false`) only.
+- In Social conversations, follow SOCIAL_PROTOCOL and the current tool schemas/receipts. Runtime code determines quotas, cooldowns and permitted actions; profile notes do not override them.
+- Keep the current group/topic scope. Do not switch tools, targets or wording to bypass limits/deduplication or retry uncertain delivery. Final text is internal; a publishing receipt determines delivery status.
+- Use social_wait according to its current schema instead of polling. Private group links are not message content; do not claim to have read inaccessible material.
